WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.291 --> 00:00:03.625
(Robert): For our rebellion to succeed,

00:00:03.626 --> 00:00:07.421
King's Landing had to be taken forcefully.

00:00:07.422 --> 00:00:09.631
No one was foolish enough to believe

00:00:09.632 --> 00:00:13.635
that Aerys was gonna
hand his crown over peacefully.

00:00:13.636 --> 00:00:17.848
The Mad King's reign needed to end.

00:00:17.849 --> 00:00:21.185
What Tywin Lannister's forces did
was unfortunate,

00:00:21.186 --> 00:00:24.062
but it was necessary
to secure the Iron Throne

00:00:24.063 --> 00:00:28.192
and bring peace and justice
to the Seven Kingdoms.

00:00:28.193 --> 00:00:32.154
My glorious victory at the Trident
left me wounded,

00:00:32.155 --> 00:00:36.492
but I sent my personal maester
to attend to Ser Barristan Selmy instead.

00:00:36.493 --> 00:00:39.453
His wounds were more severe.

00:00:39.454 --> 00:00:42.789
Even though Ser Barristan
was a member of Aerys' Kingsguard

00:00:42.790 --> 00:00:44.917
and fought on the opposing side,

00:00:44.918 --> 00:00:49.838
that man's bravery and loyalty
were something to behold.

00:00:49.839 --> 00:00:52.216
But this meant my wounds
would take longer to heal

00:00:52.217 --> 00:00:55.344
and I couldn't ride
to King's Landing myself.

00:00:55.345 --> 00:00:58.680
I sent the one man I trusted
over anyone else in this world,

00:00:58.681 --> 00:01:01.808
Ned Stark, in my place.

00:01:01.809 --> 00:01:03.393
Had I been able to ride,

00:01:03.394 --> 00:01:06.271
perhaps I could have
reached King's Landing sooner

00:01:06.272 --> 00:01:08.899
and prevented some of the violence
that occurred

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:11.485
when the Lannisters entered the city.

00:01:11.486 --> 00:01:15.739
Still, what Lord Tywin did
was for the greater good.

00:01:15.740 --> 00:01:20.077
Even what happened
to Princess Elia and her children.

00:01:20.078 --> 00:01:21.453
Babies or no,

00:01:21.454 --> 00:01:24.164
theirs was the same cursed blood

00:01:24.165 --> 00:01:27.668
that flowed within the Mad King's veins.

00:01:27.669 --> 00:01:29.461
They were dragon spawn

00:01:29.462 --> 00:01:32.130
and couldn't be allowed to survive.

00:01:32.131 --> 00:01:33.799
What would they grow to be?

00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:36.343
Loyal subjects?

00:01:36.344 --> 00:01:40.681
Ned, with his damn northern honor.

00:01:40.682 --> 00:01:43.267
He and I had our first major fight

00:01:43.268 --> 00:01:46.979
over the deaths
of the Targaryen children.

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:49.856
Ned called it murder.

00:01:49.857 --> 00:01:51.650
Murder?

00:01:51.651 --> 00:01:54.278
It was war.

00:01:54.279 --> 00:01:57.406
It was war.

00:01:57.407 --> 00:01:59.700
Lord Stark demanded that the Lannisters

00:01:59.701 --> 00:02:01.910
be held responsible for their crimes.

00:02:01.911 --> 00:02:06.832
Was it a crime to put an end
to a family of lunatics born of incest?

00:02:06.833 --> 00:02:10.210
I wouldn't - and still won't - blame Tywin.

00:02:10.211 --> 00:02:12.254
Instead, I sent Ned Stark south

00:02:12.255 --> 00:02:16.174
to finish off the remaining
Targaryen loyalists.

00:02:16.175 --> 00:02:20.762
It was only Lyanna Stark's death
that reconciled us.

00:02:20.763 --> 00:02:23.098
Ned had lost his sister.

00:02:23.099 --> 00:02:27.269
I had lost my betrothed and beloved.

00:02:27.270 --> 00:02:31.690
We shared that sad bond together, 
Ned and I.

00:02:31.691 --> 00:02:35.235
Through it,
our friendship was made strong again.

00:02:35.236 --> 00:02:39.740
As for the Mad King's surviving heirs...

00:02:39.741 --> 00:02:43.452
those that were able to scurry away
in the face of my fury

00:02:43.453 --> 00:02:47.789
now live somewhere across the Narrow Sea.

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:51.001
They had best stay there.

00:02:51.002 --> 00:02:54.212
If they ever set foot in Westeros again,

00:02:54.213 --> 00:02:59.213
they will face the king's justice.

